      "detail": {
        "type": "comment",
        "comment": {
          "forge": "gitea",
          "instance": "gitea.com",
          "thread": {
            "forge": "gitea",
            "instance": "gitea.com",
            "repo": {
              "forge": "gitea",
              "instance": "gitea.com",
              "owner": "gitea",
              "name": "tea",
              "externalId": "550"
            },
            "kind": "pull_request",
            "number": "1144"
          },
          "id": "1766914"
        },
        "body": "For context, here is how the wait compares across versions. Measured against a gitea.com repository with push access and no PR template; the `main` and PR numbers are medians of 10 alternating runs.\n\n| Version | Before first prompt | Between prompts | Total wait |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| v0.15 release | ~0.15 s | ~0.9 s + ~1.2 s | ~2.2 s, split across 3 places |\n| current `main` | ~3.1 s | none | ~3.1 s |\n| `main` + this PR | ~2.2 s | none | ~2.2 s |\n| + template paths probed concurrently (experiment, not in this PR) | ~1.3 s | none | ~1.3 s |\n\nSince the Cobra rewrite, the form loads all of its data up front. That removes the pauses between prompts but makes the initial wait longer than in the release. This PR brings the total back to roughly the release level, now paid once up front.\n\nThe remaining bottleneck is the template lookup, which probes six paths sequentially. Probing them concurrently and still picking the first match in priority order gives the last row, but it always sends six requests instead of stopping at the first hit, which the existing tests assert. I kept that out of this PR and am happy to send it as a follow-up if that trade-off is acceptable.\n\n**Update:** the follow-up is now open as #1145."
      },
